From: fixture <fixture@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] fuzz: outermost context line altered

Same change as good.patch, but the outermost (last) context line is
altered while all remaining 3/3 context stays correct. GNU patch trims
only trailing context when fuzzing, so this cannot apply at --fuzz=0
and applies from fuzz=1 up. Verified: patch -p1 --fuzz=0 fails,
--fuzz=1 applies at the intended spot. Note: quilt prints its
"Hunk #N succeeded at ... with fuzz ..." diagnostics on stdout, so
failure tests must capture stdout.
--- a/hello.c
+++ b/hello.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #include <stdio.h>

+/* fuzz patch line */
 void hello(void)
 {
 	printf("hello from the mini tree\n");
 } /* outermost context line altered for the fuzz fixture */
